Do you have a djembe sitting in the corner that needs a repair with a popped skin, or a terrible sound?

The weather has been tough on our loved ones over the warmer months and we need to make sure they stay dry and out of hot, humid cars or rooms in the house. The warm and cold temperatures will affect the sound of your drum and quite possibly you need a bit of a tune up. It may even be time to have your drum skin replaced!

To get your drum sounding beautiful again, we can do a reskin which includes a cow or goat hide, new ropes, oiled shell and of course a tune up. We also have a new bunch of dundun shells which are ready to be made up, adopted and taken to a new home. If you are in the market for a new djembe or dundun set, send us an email or drop us a call to find out what we have in stock.

Just recently we prepared an order for a local disability and community organisation in Nambour. Here is a snapshot of part of the package they ordered.

